3 0 obj
<< /Length 1045 >>
stream
BT /F2 16 Tf 50 775 Td (CS302 Operating Systems) Tj ET
BT /F2 14 Tf 50 752 Td (Unit 2: CPU Scheduling) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 50 732 Td (Northfield Institute of Technology - Dr. Kavita Mehta) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 50 691 Td (1. Why scheduling matters) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 50 671 Td (The CPU scheduler picks which ready process runs next. Goals: high CPU utilisation,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 50 651 Td (high throughput, and low waiting, turnaround and response times.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 50 610 Td (2. First-Come, First-Served \(FCFS\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 50 590 Td (Processes run in arrival order. Simple, but a long job delays all short ones behind it) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 50 570 Td (\(the convoy effect\), so average waiting time can be high.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 50 529 Td (3. Shortest Job First \(SJF\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 50 509 Td (Runs the process with the shortest next CPU burst. It gives the minimum average waiting) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 50 489 Td (time for a given set of processes, but needs burst lengths in advance and can starve long jobs.) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
