5 0 obj
<< /Length 930 >>
stream
BT /F2 12 Tf 50 779 Td (4. Round Robin \(RR\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 50 759 Td (Each process gets a fixed time quantum, then goes to the back of the ready queue.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 50 739 Td (Good response time for interactive systems. Too small a quantum adds context-switch) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 50 719 Td (overhead; too large and RR behaves like FCFS.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 50 678 Td (5. Worked example) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 50 658 Td (P1 = 8, P2 = 4, P3 = 2 \(all arrive at 0\). FCFS average wait = 6.67; SJF average wait = 2.67;) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 50 638 Td (RR \(quantum 2\) average wait = 5.33. Draw a Gantt chart for each to check your answer.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 50 597 Td (6. Key terms) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 50 577 Td (Waiting time = turnaround time - burst time. Turnaround time = completion time - arrival time.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 50 557 Td (Preemptive schedulers \(RR, preemptive SJF\) can interrupt a running process.) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
